                        "entry_id": "ef14e3c3-71ed-3167-a83f-3ae71baa3d6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A cerebroid ganglion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b28615e5-36fc-427f-a6e6-10ab9afb02b5",
                                "sense_id": "290c6795-477c-3910-8dc6-13d3444e678e",
                                "text": "The first cerebroid or capitis cerebroida, is composed of two hemispheres; from these arise, in perfect insects, several pairs of nerves;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8633799-3063-4d9e-9dda-af6be800965d",
                                "sense_id": "290c6795-477c-3910-8dc6-13d3444e678e",
                                "text": "The cerebroids communicate with each other across the median line ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89b05326-a7ec-4f21-9a74-c918e8601be5",
                                "sense_id": "290c6795-477c-3910-8dc6-13d3444e678e",
                                "text": "The cerebroid supplies nerves to the tentacles, mouth, and lips."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31f38e9d-b9ca-3343-831a-b332d91b8b4c",
                        "entry_id": "ef14e3c3-71ed-3167-a83f-3ae71baa3d6a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An organoid (mass of cells grown in vitro) cultured from cerebral cells."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26dbe328-53e6-4ca3-bcab-386a1f237982",
                                "sense_id": "31f38e9d-b9ca-3343-831a-b332d91b8b4c",
                                "text": "At this stage, of coures, the crew of cerebroids can be removed when the hardware becomes obsolete , and transferred to a different type of ship ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8a759d8-5564-46d3-923e-a2b91da9f797",
                                "sense_id": "31f38e9d-b9ca-3343-831a-b332d91b8b4c",
                                "text": "The notion of life inherent in the development of cerebroids and gastruloids will be presented as the moral status of these two special organoids is discussed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2afb236b-5e81-43b7-ae13-3453c913c1d9",
                                "sense_id": "31f38e9d-b9ca-3343-831a-b332d91b8b4c",
                                "text": "Outcomes may include timely implementation of technology where it is demanded, low incidence of lawsuits surrounding alleged misuse of the technology, government funding of research into the ethics and biology of animals augmented with human cerebroids, intersection between authors writing for scholarly and public audiences, and results from research on public sentiments.."
                            }
                        ]
